{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Session state at handoff — 2026-09-19T00:30Z\n\nOrchestrator session driving the autonomous delivery loop. This entry records durable state so a\nsuccessor session can resume without re-deriving anything.\n\n### Gerrit changes in flight\n\n| Change | Ticket | Patchset / commit | LLM-Review | Verified | State |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2986 | `0eba-cfd8-34b0-4cb7` | merged | +1 | +1 | MERGED, `origin/main` = `c4c0702878` |\n| 2987 | `f5ac-391c-ec70-4fa9` | ps2 / `0d9ad5b00bb` | **+1** | running | awaiting CI |\n| 2984 | `8d27-d715-0611-48e3` | ps6 / `bad9dfd1d76` | **-1** | none | agent covering branches |\n\n### Push and submit both require the admin credential\n\n`rebar-review-bot` cannot upload a patchset whose committer is anyone but itself, and cannot\nsubmit. Established by evidence, not inference: every patchset on 2984, 2986 and 2987 was\nuploaded by `Administrator`. A push attempted with the bot credential is rejected with\n`you lack 'forge committer' permission`. `forgeCommitter` on `All-Projects` `refs/heads/*` is\ngranted only to `Project-Owners` and `Administrators`; the bot holds neither. Full ACL state and\nthree candidate remedies are on ticket `despairing-wholesome-gelada` (`e8d8-e2a1-c826-409f`),\nwhich is a human decision and deliberately not made.\n\nPush and submit therefore both use the admin credential from SSM\n`/rebar/prod/gerrit-admin-password`, supplied through an inline git credential helper that\nreferences variable NAMES so no secret reaches the process list.\n\n### 2984 has a convergence problem, not a defect problem\n\nPatchsets 4, 5 and 6 each took `LLM-Review -1`. Each round the reviewer named one or two\nnewly-added-but-untested branches, those exact tests were added, and the next round named\ndifferent ones. Fixing the named instance is not converging.\n\nA background agent is now closing the class rather than the instance: measure branch coverage\nover `handler.py`, intersect with the lines `git diff origin/main...HEAD` actually introduces,\nand cover every uncovered branch — including the advisory `_seed_for` cache-token branches, so\nthey cannot become round 7. Teeth-checks are required on every test, because stubbing the\nfunction under test is precisely how these gaps were introduced.\n\n### A design change was made and then deliberately reverted\n\nAn earlier round treated `handler.py:579` as a dual-signal outage deadlock and changed the\nhandler to release the cap after one UTC day of telemetry outage. That was wrong and has been\nfully reverted. It is not a deadlock: the release condition is\n`spend < THRESHOLD_USD and not signal_unavailable`, so when telemetry recovers the signal\nbecomes available, spend reads a real value, and the deny detaches normally. The cap stays\nattached only for the duration of the outage, which is correct fail-closed behaviour for a\ncircuit breaker. The reviewer files this as an ADVISORY and it must stay unactioned. The enforce\ncondition must remain `if any_attached and spend < THRESHOLD_USD and not signal_unavailable:`.\n\n### Two closes are pre-audited and blocked on different things\n\nBoth pending closes carried latent gate failures that would each have burned a full\nreview-and-close cycle to discover. Both were found and recorded before spending anything.\n\n`0eba` / `peaceable-chunky-harvestmen` — `in_progress`, change merged. `file_impact` declared 2\npaths against the merged commit's 8; corrected to the real 8. All 9 acceptance criteria are\nstill unchecked; a read-only agent is gathering evidence for each, including a full `make\nverify`. The `file_impact` widening invalidated the plan attestation, so a fresh plan review is\nrequired before the close.\n\n**Sequencing that matters:** do NOT start `0eba`'s plan review until its criteria boxes are\nticked. Ticking them edits the description, which is material a plan review pins, so reviewing\nfirst would invalidate the review and cost a second full pass.\n\n`f5ac` / `stable-jobless-coot` — `in_progress`, change at ps2 awaiting Verified. 5 criteria, 0\nchecked. Two are proven from the diff and the evidence is recorded on the ticket: the pack limit\nis untouched and the comparison survives the step split with the same operator and the same\nfail-closed `exit 1`, and no monitoring mechanism was added. The other three assert what a real\nrun does and stay open until the change is green. `file_impact` declares 1 path against 4\ntouched; widening is deliberately deferred until the change lands, because CI feedback could\nstill alter the file set.\n\n### `contained-blue-nandine` is planned and under review\n\n`8c79-5cf4-0773-4afc`, P1, still open and unclaimed. `make worktree` is broken for every\nsession. A plan review is running now.\n\nRoot cause confirmed by reading the target: `@set -e; \\` ends in a continuation but the next\nline is an `@#` comment, so make joins them and the shell parses `<branch>` in the comment text\nas an input redirect.\n\nA second defect sits behind the first and the remedy must address both together: because the\ncomment block terminates the continued line, `set -e` is already stranded on its own line and\nnever governs the body. Bug 1738's protection — which exists so a failed `make venv` cannot be\nreported as \"✓ worktree ready\" — is therefore already detached. Relocating the comments without\nrejoining `set -e` would restore the target while silently leaving it able to report success\nover a failed provisioning step.\n\nThe default directory has been unwritable twice. Ticket `9b4a-89fb-3328-497e` moved it from a\nsibling of the checkout to `$HOME/worktrees/`, which is outside the sandbox boundary as well.\nThree conventions are in circulation and no two agree: `AGENTS.md` line 441 says `../<name>`,\nthe Makefile says `$HOME/worktrees/rebar/<name>`, and all 12 worktrees that actually exist are\nunder `.rebar/worktrees/`, which is covered by `.gitignore` so nested worktrees never show as\nuntracked. Operator decision taken: adopt `.rebar/worktrees/<name>` and update both documents to\nmatch.\n\nThe guard was also redesigned. Asserting \"no `@#` on a continuation line\" tests one token;\nexpanding the recipe with `make -n` and feeding it to `sh -n` catches the entire class of\ncontinuation and quoting defects and depends on no CI provider.\n\n### Spend\n\nThe Bedrock day rolls at 00:00 UTC, which is 17:00 local — not local midnight. Yesterday closed\nat roughly two thirds of the cap without tripping. The day has rolled, the pause is cleared, and\ntoday is well under the warning level. `ce_spend` lags uselessly; read the real figure from the\nlambda decision log rather than the SSM state parameter.\n\n### Monitoring\n\nOne alarm outstanding, `rebar-docker-buildkit-cache-high`, already tracked as `3057` and its\nBuildKit GC discriminator still UNVERIFIED. The two CI failures visible are both known: 2987\npatchset 1, whose fix is now at ps2, and `Verify Authorship Identity`, which is the `f5ac`\ndefect itself.\n\n### Owed to the operator, one at a time\n\nThe `48bd` fix direction; the rate-card decisions; the S2 production-swap NO-GO gating epic\n`polite-antivirus-bedbug`; and the fate of unpushed local commit `7b92d821718`, which still sits\non the shared main checkout and may be operator WIP."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789777959667446670,"uuid":"8d0adf67-7eeb-43b5-a3a0-eac2b1fedf2e"}